      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "I AM A ROCKSTAR (1) sets the standard despite a plain fifth in Class B company at Leinster, as this looks a more suitable Mdn and he is third-up on a quick back-up. His Leonora fourth two runs ago reads well enough for this, and his record on good tracks gives him the most rounded profile of the main hopes. INSPIRATIONAL MAC (3) is the immediate threat after running second over 1000m at Leinster at generous odds, with third-up fitness in his favour, but four unplaced 1200m attempts leave a genuine query. WILLYABRUP (2) finished closer than I AM A ROCKSTAR behind Gingeriffic last week and gets the same class drop, though a 25-start maiden record makes him easier to see in the placings than as a clear winner. SAMBUCA ROSE (4) has race fitness and a recent Open third at Landor to lean on, but her Leinster fifth was a sizeable backward step and she has to rebound quickly. UNRULY DAME (5) rounds them out.",
